From 76b567e55335884d3fb778ddb014b720f1e07f7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JC Fillion-Robin <jcfr@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:52:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Acknowledge intentional Cargo source builds

Treat the Cargo fallback as an expected configuration when building this HoloMQ-patched dependency from source. Replace the generic production warning with a status message that identifies the selected build path.

This changes diagnostics only; Cargo target selection and Rust artifact generation remain unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [holoscan specific]

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index cdb80336..0d882a52 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -153,11 +153,8 @@ endif()
 if(RUST_BUILD_ARTIFACT_PATH AND NOT "${RUST_BUILD_ARTIFACT_PATH}" STREQUAL "" )
     add_subdirectory(iceoryx2-c)
 else()
-    message(WARNING
-        "Using cargo to build the Rust part of iceoryx2. "
-        "This is fine for development but for production, it is "
-        "recommended to use an existing installation with\n"
-        "'-DRUST_BUILD_ARTIFACT_PATH=/full/path/to/iceoryx2/target/release'!"
+    message(STATUS
+        "Building the Rust part of the HoloMQ-patched iceoryx2 dependency with cargo"
     )
 
     set(RUST_BUILD_TYPE "release")
